 "notes": "Regenerated in full against base=9f1369b (main's tip after SEC-0052 merged concurrently \u2014 the prior receipt's base, 30c6f5c, is now two commits stale) rather than patched, since the impact set itself changed (a new receipt: entity appeared, pulled in only because both this PR and SEC-0052 touch apps/api/test/assembly/mutation-results.json for unrelated reasons). \n\nHistory this receipt closes out: two real problems surfaced only by CI's real database, not by this sandbox's default (no DATABASE_URL) jest run: (1) TasksService.delete() hit Prisma P2003 (task_execution_state FK, onDelete: Restrict) for any task that ever entered in_progress \u2014 fixed by converting it to a 409 ConflictException. (2) task_execution_transitions and task_outbox_events are DB-trigger-enforced append-only \u2014 transitively making task_execution_attempts/state, and therefore the task itself, permanently undeletable once any transition is recorded; a genuine, deliberate, previously-unexercised consequence of this card's wiring. tasks-agent-scope.e2e.spec.ts's cleanup was fixed to exclude such tasks from its own deleteMany rather than try to delete rows the database will never allow deleted. Both independently re-verified against a real local Postgres, not just assumed fixed. \n\nA separate CI blocker (self-hosted runner user not in the docker group, so the Postgres service container never started) was diagnosed and fixed by the operator mid-session, not by this branch \u2014 confirmed by re-running lint-and-test after the fix and getting a clean pass. \n\nThe 15 not_measured entities from the earlier version of this receipt are resolved here per DEC-AUP-0010 (no operator gates): 13 apps/web nodes via a real read-only canary probe against production, 2 deployable_unit nodes via a typed, owned, expiring exemption since can-i-deploy is a deploy-time question this repo's own `deploy` CI job already owns.",
